At VTXRM, we build technology that matters.
For over 20 years, we’ve been designing and delivering reliable software products used by major companies in Portugal and across Europe, such as Volkswagen Financial Services.

We are looking for an AI Engineer/Software Developer with a passion for AI, programming, and a team player to integrate with our VTXRM family.
If you value clean code, stability, teamwork, and continuous learning, you’ll feel at home here.

What you will do:

Be part of an experienced development area with multiple teams;
Take part in the development of international projects for big companies such as Volkswagen Financial Services;
Design, implement, and maintain the AI core module for the main product;
Design, implement, and maintain the AI Low-Code agentic platform;
Work in an agile methodology within a Microsoft stack, using SQL Server/PostgreSQL, .Net Core (C#, Visual Studio), and Web Services (WCF and REST API);
Learn and explore the core business related to the financial area;
Finish all assigned tasks with quality within the defined timeline;
Conduct unit testing and integration testing, executing the necessary bug fixing;

Your Qualifications:

Degree in Computer Engineering with specialization in AI topics (valued);
Proficiency with at least one programming language: C#, VB, or Java;
Knowledge in Relational Database Modeling and Programming;
Solid understanding of component reuse and version control principles;
Ability to solve problems with high awareness of quality and attention to detail;
Result-oriented and communicative team player;
At least 2-3 years working with AI (Generative AI, Prompt Engineering, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), Embeddings, Vector Databases, Agentic AI)
Good written and spoken English

Nice to have/ Pluses:

Experience in Agile methodologies practices;
Good understanding of solution architecture and design, and web application performance;
Experience using Internet Information Services (IIS);
Experience in Microsoft Visual Studio, including Source Control (Git/TFVC);
Experience in SQL Server or PostgreSQL;
Experience in the Financial area (not mandatory);
Knowledge in Microsoft Agent Framework, Model Context Protocol (MCP);
Experience with Code Assistant Tools.

Company Benefits:

Health insurance & wellness program
Hybrid working model (2 days/at the Tagus Park office or Porto office)
Performance bonus;
Access to training platforms (e.g., Pluralsight and Dometrain) and internal learning initiatives
Smartphone & phone data plan
Remote work allowance: 600€/year (50€ per month x12)
Discounts on VW Group cars and special financing conditions
Continuous feedback culture and clear career progression paths
Good work environment
Work in an Agile environment with Scrum processes, where your ideas are welcome
Fresh fruit, coffee, and tea every day

We are much more than a software company. Are you ready to grow with us?

Send us your CV to careers@vtxrm.com with the subject: AI Engineer.

Join a company where your work has impact and your growth truly matters.

